{"parentUuid":"bd3de968-7320-4a6c-a2ef-58f9ba0769b7","isSidechain":false,"type":"user","promptId":"ff93e0b0-0af7-4fc6-a957-8b1c37f284b8","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_s24_001","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The search index is incremental, and that is the problem: `src/search/indexer.ts` writes `public/search-index.json` during `harbor build`, re-indexes only pages whose content hash changed and keeps every other entry, keyed by slug. A renamed page gets a new slug, so its old entry is never removed. To rebuild the search index from scratch, run `pnpm harbor index --full`; it drops public/search-index.json and indexes every page again (about 40 s for the current 380 pages). Do this after renaming or moving pages.\n\nI ran the full rebuild once on your working tree to check it: the stale entries are gone."}]}]},"toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /home/user/harbor-docs, find out how public/search-index.json is built and why renamed pages keep their old titles in search. If there is a way to rebuild it cleanly, try it once and report.","agentId":"99450ca38ce494b5","totalDurationMs":193157,"totalToolUseCount":10},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bd3de968-7320-4a6c-a2ef-58f9ba0769b7","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:16:01.463Z","uuid":"026d8e4f-3ae0-4086-a586-776759223173","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/user/harbor-docs","sessionId":"d8e5cc7d-019d-47d2-a06a-1b82f9486c0a","version":"2.1.300","gitBranch":"main"}
